Lets WantList::insert replace a want whose commit is in flight with a newer
version again; only a reset still holds its path, as before f7a7deb (§7.5: at
most one commit in flight per path). The older commit still lands, its report
no longer matches the want and is dropped, and the next scan finds the landed
file as a local change nobody made. The other half of f7a7deb, a commit's
deadline warning instead of releasing the path, is left as it is. The only
seed in 0 to 9,999 that fails with this patch does so through I4's check of
a copy under a directory displaced twice, and passes once that check also
accepts the place the copy was made, so the patch names the rule's unit test.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_version_arriving_during_a_commit_waits_for_its_report

